{"id": "EUVD-2026-95083", "enisaUuid": "a462346b-586d-311d-9660-867fc418758e", "description": "FFmpeg through 9.0.2 contains a stack exhaustion vulnerability in av_encryption_init_info_free() in libavutil/encryption_info.c, which recursively frees AVEncryptionInitInfo linked lists built by the MOV demuxer's mov_read_pssh(). Attackers can supply a crafted MP4 file with tens of thousands of small pssh boxes to exhaust the stack and crash the process, while also causing quadratic CPU consumption.", "datePublished": "2026-10-08T15:28:43", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-08T17:51:49", "baseScore": 5.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://code.ffmpeg.org/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/pulls/24593", "https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/blob/n9.0.2/libavutil/encryption_info.c#L219-L231", "https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/blob/n9.0.2/libavformat/mov.c#L8070", "https://ffmpeg.org/", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/ffmpeg-through-9.0.2-stack-exhaustion-via-recursive-free-of-pssh-boxes"], "aliases": ["GHSA-rp4v-7m3g-89vg", "CVE-2026-107678"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.09, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "5f44bf6b-26b2-3ae7-8556-513c5a5cff34", "product": {"name": "FFmpeg", "vendor": {"name": "FFMPEG"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22649.0.2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "5ea06e40-3e6c-30ff-af90-587f67a2b53a", "vendor": {"name": "FFMPEG"}}], "isExploited": false}